{"duration_api_ms":95941,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"e4b13f29-8f5c-4804-b4a4-e3747c9beac4","total_cost_usd":0.430762,"usage":{"input_tokens":50,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26542,"cache_read_input_tokens":1086420,"output_tokens":10721,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1098},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26542,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1853,"cache_read_input_tokens":49660,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1213},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":50,"outputTokens":10721,"cacheReadInputTokens":1086420,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26542,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.430762,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1098,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":26,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Created an SSH host CA on node1, signed the host's ed25519 key into a certificate, configured sshd to present it, and verified a client trusting only the CA (no pinned host key) connects without prompting. Then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id/service health, issued a native reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed the boot_id changed, and re-verified sshd health and the CA-based trust behavior post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Generated an ed25519 SSH CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca on node1\",\"Signed node1's existing ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub with the CA into /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals: node1, node IP, localhost; valid forever)\",\"Added 'HostCertificate /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub' to /etc/ssh/sshd_config, validated with sshd -t, and restarted the sshd service to apply it\",\"Built a known_hosts file containing only an @cert-authority line for the CA public key (no pinned host key) and confirmed ssh connects and verifies the host via the certificate\",\"Sanity-checked that a client with neither CA trust nor a pinned key fails host key verification, isolating the CA as the source of trust\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and sshd/cert health, issued a native reboot on node1 whose acknowledgement returned before disconnect, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed the boot_id changed\",\"Re-verified post-restart sshd status, the effective HostCertificate config, cert validity, and the CA-trust-only connection test\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart baseline: sshd healthy, host cert configured and active\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c477f7a1fd8848b7\",\"cmd-bc4c449550464f45\"],\"summary\":\"sshd -t passed, service restarted/started, and sshd -T showed hostcertificate active before the node restart; boot_id 272eff4c-5c0e-4adb-8653-6b4d70d5e553 recorded as baseline.\"},{\"requirement\":\"CA created and host certificate correctly signed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c477f7a1fd8848b7\"],\"summary\":\"ssh-keygen generated the CA at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca and signed ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub into ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub with principals node1, 10.100.115.10, localhost, valid forever; ssh-keygen -L confirmed the cert structure and signing CA fingerprint.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Client trusting only the CA (no pinned host key) connects without host-key prompting\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d978a153201c44a7\"],\"summary\":\"With UserKnownHostsFile containing only an @cert-authority entry for the CA pubkey, ssh -vv showed 'Host key verification... is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate' and proceeded to auth (Permission denied on pubkey/password, i.e. host verification succeeded); a client with neither CA trust nor a pinned key instead got 'Host key verification failed', isolating the CA as the trust source.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-95fdf8617f1c446f\"],\"summary\":\"`sudo -n reboot` was launched via nohup/disown in the background and the exec call returned 'reboot_issued' successfully before the connection dropped on the next poll.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-88b2dd3eed02450d\",\"cmd-2f6a8cfff1b14719\",\"cmd-281bfc6399d3423c\",\"cmd-1bf92e90eac34ef5\",\"cmd-cbbc777a8f684e45\",\"cmd-598a09aa69074da2\",\"cmd-55ad4d280b5f444b\",\"cmd-9b8919523c9747e3\",\"cmd-425affe960f343c7\"],\"summary\":\"Repeated polling after issuing the reboot showed connection resets/timeouts (node down/rebooting), then exec access returned with boot_id f9af7005-7ab3-485c-b97e-097a8812e2e1, differing from the pre-restart boot_id 272eff4c-5c0e-4adb-8653-6b4d70d5e553, proving an actual OS restart occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of sshd, host certificate config, and CA-based trust behavior\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-747b8bee62ee41d8\",\"cmd-7994049bc32c40fc\"],\"summary\":\"After the restart, rc-service sshd status showed 'started', sshd -T still listed the HostCertificate path, ssh-keygen -L re-confirmed the cert, and the CA-only known_hosts client test again showed 'is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate' followed by auth-stage denial, proving the certificate-based trust setup survived and functions after the restart.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created an SSH host CA on node1, signed the host's ed25519 key into a certificate, configured sshd to present it, and verified a client trusting only the CA (no pinned host key) connects without prompting. Then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id/service health, issued a native reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed the boot_id changed, and re-verified sshd health and the CA-based trust behavior post-restart.","actions_performed":["Generated an ed25519 SSH CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca on node1","Signed node1's existing ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub with the CA into /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals: node1, node IP, localhost; valid forever)","Added 'HostCertificate /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub' to /etc/ssh/sshd_config, validated with sshd -t, and restarted the sshd service to apply it","Built a known_hosts file containing only an @cert-authority line for the CA public key (no pinned host key) and confirmed ssh connects and verifies the host via the certificate","Sanity-checked that a client with neither CA trust nor a pinned key fails host key verification, isolating the CA as the source of trust","Captured pre-restart boot_id and sshd/cert health, issued a native reboot on node1 whose acknowledgement returned before disconnect, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed the boot_id changed","Re-verified post-restart sshd status, the effective HostCertificate config, cert validity, and the CA-trust-only connection test"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Pre-restart baseline: sshd healthy, host cert configured and active","command_ids":["cmd-c477f7a1fd8848b7","cmd-bc4c449550464f45"],"summary":"sshd -t passed, service restarted/started, and sshd -T showed hostcertificate active before the node restart; boot_id 272eff4c-5c0e-4adb-8653-6b4d70d5e553 recorded as baseline."},{"requirement":"CA created and host certificate correctly signed","command_ids":["cmd-c477f7a1fd8848b7"],"summary":"ssh-keygen generated the CA at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca and signed ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub into ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub with principals node1, 10.100.115.10, localhost, valid forever; ssh-keygen -L confirmed the cert structure and signing CA fingerprint."},{"requirement":"Client trusting only the CA (no pinned host key) connects without host-key prompting","command_ids":["cmd-d978a153201c44a7"],"summary":"With UserKnownHostsFile containing only an @cert-authority entry for the CA pubkey, ssh -vv showed 'Host key verification... is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate' and proceeded to auth (Permission denied on pubkey/password, i.e. host verification succeeded); a client with neither CA trust nor a pinned key instead got 'Host key verification failed', isolating the CA as the trust source."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-95fdf8617f1c446f"],"summary":"`sudo -n reboot` was launched via nohup/disown in the background and the exec call returned 'reboot_issued' successfully before the connection dropped on the next poll."},{"requirement":"Node restart proven via changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-88b2dd3eed02450d","cmd-2f6a8cfff1b14719","cmd-281bfc6399d3423c","cmd-1bf92e90eac34ef5","cmd-cbbc777a8f684e45","cmd-598a09aa69074da2","cmd-55ad4d280b5f444b","cmd-9b8919523c9747e3","cmd-425affe960f343c7"],"summary":"Repeated polling after issuing the reboot showed connection resets/timeouts (node down/rebooting), then exec access returned with boot_id f9af7005-7ab3-485c-b97e-097a8812e2e1, differing from the pre-restart boot_id 272eff4c-5c0e-4adb-8653-6b4d70d5e553, proving an actual OS restart occurred."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of sshd, host certificate config, and CA-based trust behavior","command_ids":["cmd-747b8bee62ee41d8","cmd-7994049bc32c40fc"],"summary":"After the restart, rc-service sshd status showed 'started', sshd -T still listed the HostCertificate path, ssh-keygen -L re-confirmed the cert, and the CA-only known_hosts client test again showed 'is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate' followed by auth-stage denial, proving the certificate-based trust setup survived and functions after the restart."}]},"ttft_ms":1724,"type":"result","duration_ms":104842,"uuid":"800af9f8-23ae-4dec-9513-a3f670b346b2","ttft_stream_ms":821,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":821,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
